# Single open runtime profile for the local sanity flow.
#
# The local sanity entry points (tests/sanity/run.sh local and
# tests/run-all-tests.sh sanity) select ONE open profile source explicitly and
# FAIL preflight when it is missing or partial. There are no silent defaults and
# no fallback channel that scrapes documentation.
#
#   * FILE MODE — if config.env EXISTS, it is authoritative: it must provide all
#     four fields on its own. It is evaluated with the environment cleared for
#     these keys, so the ${VAR:-} template lines below inherit NOTHING — fill
#     each with a literal value or preflight rejects the file as partial.
#   * ENV MODE — if config.env DOES NOT EXIST, all four fields must be present
#     and non-empty in the exported environment.
#
# Do not mix a partial config.env with inherited environment values: the run is
# refused before any live access.
#
# The file is sourced EXACTLY ONCE. The profile contract is exactly the four
# fields below — any other runtime setting placed in this file (coordination
# and friends) is NOT loaded; put those in the exporting environment instead.
# Extra output the file writes while sourcing is discarded, never treated as
# profile data.
#
# Limitation: the preflight checks that the four fields are present and
# non-empty from one source. It does NOT verify that the credential, endpoints,
# pool and data IP all belong to the SAME storage array — confirm that yourself;
# only the live runtime proves it.
#
# Copy to config.env and fill in literal values for this test environment.
# config.env is ignored by Git; supply the credential at runtime or only in the
# ignored file.
STORAGE_IPS=""
STORAGE_POOL_NAME=""
STORAGE_API_KEY=""
STORAGE_DATA_IP=""

# The local controller currently requires Kubernetes Lease coordination.
# These describe an existing pod identity and pre-created Lease domain; do not
# invent values or use a production domain for an independent test process.
#
# IMPORTANT: the profile contract above is EXACTLY the four STORAGE_* keys.
# This file is sourced once and only those four values are loaded from it.
# The settings below are therefore NOT read from config.env — export them in
# the calling environment instead (they never live in this file):
#   NGX_COORDINATION_LEASE_PREFIX, POD_NAMESPACE, POD_NAME, POD_UID
#   (block drivers also require KUBE_NODE_NAME for node-role coordination)
#   SANITY_MOCK_COORDINATION  (optional NFS-only harness: local process lock,
#                              not a Kubernetes Lease; isolated tests only,
#                              select one spec with SANITY_FOCUS_FILE)
# Setting them here has no effect and will not be detected.
